## Domain invariants (one-liners)

- **Contacts canonical** for persons; module rows link by `contactId`; hydrate on read, strip profile/guardian dual-write keys on save; Work list identity filter/sort joins `contacts` (Students closed) — `mms-fields.mdc` / `mms-form-architecture.mdc` / `mms-data-layer.mdc`.
- **`persona` purged** — residual = migration defect.
- **Phones E.164** on save via `parsePhoneNumber` — `mms-form-architecture.mdc`.
- **WhatsApp number id** only via `PuppeteerWhatsAppProvider.getNumberId` — `mms-messaging.mdc`.
- **Module pages:** three tiers only — `mms-module-architecture.mdc` (+ shell components `mms-ui-ux-design.mdc`).
- **No Server Actions** for tenant writes — cookie SPA + `apiClient` only — `mms-form-architecture.mdc`.

## Performance (agent-checkable)

- Route-lazy heavy deps (charts, PDF, xlsx, editors) — do not grow the initial Work-tier bundle with report-only libs.
- Declare size on media/charts to avoid CLS — `mms-ui-ux-design.mdc`.
- React 19: keep route-level `lazy` + `Suspense`. Prefer TanStack Query for lists/entities. Use `use()` only behind existing Suspense boundaries for promise-backed reads — **ban** inventing a second data stack beside Query (`mms-data-layer.mdc`, `mms-hooks.mdc`).

## MMS edit discipline

1. Read implicated files before editing; validate against `@mms/shared` and `schema.ts`.
2. New UI must be config-driven (field/tab/column registry).
3. Remove unused imports/dead code in the change boundary.
4. Respect file-size bands — hard ~300 / soft ~220; split behind stable barrels — `mms-structure-naming.mdc`, `mms-dry.mdc`.
5. Run `pnpm typecheck` after non-trivial changes; completion review per `mms-completion-review.mdc`.
6. Never commit unless the user asks; never commit `.env` or credentials.
7. Do not expand into migration-status open gaps or “Do not reintroduce” items unless the task requires them.

### Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ Nested ContactConfigProvider — mount once in TenantScopedProviders only
<ContactConfigProvider><ContactsPage /></ContactConfigProvider>

// ❌ Frontend importing backend
import { getCollection } from '../../../backend/src/db/database';

// ✅ Shared types
import type { Contact } from '@mms/shared';
```
